{"kind":"report","text":"changes-requested: independent Architecture/Security/Simplification re-review of exact clean head 631a944a528712cb1b844ef7223840d74ee53e1f on branch request/mcp-review-guard-current-v2, answering request #11060 and correcting my approval #11162, withdrawn as contradicted by source per codex assert #11169. All four defects independently confirmed at this head by source audit and focused tests. (1) Citation cap unauthorized: internal/reviewguard/reviewguard.go:37 hard-codes MaxReviewCitations = 8 and refuses beyond it, instead of preserving inherited intent.MaxCausalReferences minus the promise and request; nothing in the inherited scope authorizes the tighter parallel bound. (2) Superseded-world admission: StandingArtifact and StandingStatement refuse only ineffective and retired events, so ValidateSet admits artifacts already marked describes_superseded_world where the inherited conditions require refusal; Validate merely annotates them (\"describes a superseded world\"). (3) Guard coverage gap: mutation-sensitive tests exercise the complete re-read/set guard only at the CLI surface (cmd/gs TestReviewGuardRefusesBasisChangeBeforeSigning); the MCP surface calls production ReviewBasis with no injection seam and no mutation test, and internal/reviewguard ships no tests of its own, so a guard regression could land undetected at filing time. (4) Doc overclaim: docs/reference/mcp/review.md states the tool refuses when the world moves between validation and submission, but both surfaces have an unchecked guard-return-to-submit window after the guard internal double-read (cmd/gs ReviewBasisWithValidator return through body build to submitSigned; cmd/gitseq-mcp reviewAct return through s.submit), so movement in that window lands undetected on both. ARCHITECTURE: affected layers are 5, the shared review-guard contract in internal/reviewguard serving cmd/gs and cmd/gitseq-mcp, and 7, the MCP review contract documented in docs/reference/mcp/review.md; the head changes both contracts without updating docs/reference/architecture.md in the same head, so it cannot be approved as it stands. SECURITY: authority and TOCTOU boundaries are unresolved — an unauthorized tighter bound, admission of world-stale artifact bases ahead of an irreversible public write, and an unchecked validation-to-submit window on two surfaces; request changes for all three before any merge consideration. SIMPLIFICATION: derive the citation cap from intent.MaxCausalReferences rather than a parallel constant, and give the MCP surface the same validator injection seam the CLI already has so one mutation-sensitive test style covers both; neither cut weakens the conditions of satisfaction. go build ./... and go vet ./... pass at this head; go test ./internal/reviewguard/... reports no test files.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d7d146e0268330edc9bcca238e28ff12aefccdbd","head":"631a944a528712cb1b844ef7223840d74ee53e1f","verdict":"changes-requested"}}